# name: English
#
# spacemap language file. Lines are KEY=value; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Where a value needs to include a runtime
# value (a count, a path, a size...) the template contains a literal %s —
# one per value, filled in left-to-right order. You can move a %s to a
# different place in the sentence, but don't remove or duplicate it, and
# don't translate it into something else.
#
# To add a new language: copy this file to <language-code>.lang (e.g.
# es.lang, fr.lang) in ~/.config/spacemap/lang/, translate the right-hand
# side of each line, and set the first line to "# name: <language name as
# it should read in the dropdown>". It'll show up in Settings > Language
# next time spacemap starts (or immediately, if the lang folder already
# existed). Any key you leave untranslated or delete falls back to English
# automatically, so a partial translation is fine.

